description: Inline image `![alt](source "tooltip")`. Emits `<$image source="source" alt="..." tooltip="...">`. TW-markdown-plugin compat: `#`-prefix (`![alt](#Image.jpg)`) forces internal routing, `<...>` brackets wrap names with whitespace, trailing `"..."` becomes the tooltip. Priority: user-supplied body becomes `alt`, user-supplied tooltip becomes `tooltip`; when either is absent, the source tiddler's `alt-text` field fills in. Special accessibility rule for `alt`: when the user's body is 1–2 words and the source's `alt-text` is 3+ words, the source wins (richer is better for screen readers).
